# Build artifacts
*.exe
*.o
*.obj
*.a
Dist/

# Build output (out-of-source CMake build dir)
build/
!build/buildsource.bat

# Packaging output (installer + source zip — regenerated, not tracked)
packaging/output/

# FEMM model files and solver output — except the tracked example sets
*.fem
# ...except the material-library deliverables in the vendored provenance
# release: every .fem there is a FEMM library file the papers produce. Kept
# HERE, not in provenance/.gitignore, because that file is replaced wholesale
# each time a new release is dropped in.
!provenance/**/*.fem
*.fee
*.feh
*.fec
*.ans
*.anh
*.anc
!examples/*
!octavefemm/examples/*
!mathfemm/examples/*
!pyfemm/examples/*
!juliafemm/examples/*
!scifemm/examples/*

# PBC files (generated or test)
*.pbc

# Generated mesh output
*.ele
*.edge
*.node
*.neigh
*.1.poly

# Scratch files in examples
**/examples/junk.*
**/examples/temp.*

# Large result/data files
*.res

# Images, archives, documents — except the GUI icons and the manual's figures
*.pdf
# ...except the two PDFs the installers actually ship. They are build
# products, but rebuilding them needs a full TeX installation, so a
# source checkout without them means no Help > Manual on any platform
# but Windows -- which was the case until 2026-08-22.
!manual/manual.pdf
!octavefemm/manual/octavefemm.pdf
# The four build guides, for the same reason one step earlier: they are how a
# person builds this from source, and the source is exactly what they have.
# Shipping only the .tex asks someone with no working build to install TeX
# before they can read the instructions for getting a working build.
!docs/windows-build.pdf
!docs/linux-build.pdf
!docs/freebsd-build.pdf
!docs/macos-build.pdf
# The file-format references now ship too (femm-qt.iss -> {app}\docs,
# stage_extras.sh -> docs/ everywhere else), so they need the same exception
# for the same reason: a checkout without them means an installer that cannot
# be built complete, and rebuilding them needs a full TeX installation.
!docs/magnetics-file-formats.pdf
!docs/electrostatics-file-formats.pdf
!docs/heatflow-file-formats.pdf
!docs/currentflow-file-formats.pdf
# The provenance papers (vendored release in provenance/, CC BY 4.0). Named one
# by one ON PURPOSE: provenance/SOURCES.md lists third-party scans and books
# that may sit in that tree beside the papers and must never be committed, and
# a blanket !provenance/**/*.pdf would take them in. Kept here rather than in
# provenance/.gitignore, which each new release replaces. A new paper needs a
# line here.
!provenance/ceramic/ceramiccurves.pdf
!provenance/cobalt-iron/cofecurves.pdf
!provenance/iron/ironcurves.pdf
!provenance/libraries/provenance/condlib_provenance.pdf
!provenance/libraries/provenance/heatlib_provenance.pdf
!provenance/libraries/provenance/statlib_provenance.pdf
!provenance/low-carbon/bhcurves.pdf
!provenance/magnets/AlnicoProperties.pdf
!provenance/magnets/BondedNdFeB.pdf
!provenance/magnets/SinteredNdFeBProperties.pdf
!provenance/magnets/SmCoProperties.pdf
!provenance/metglas/metglascurves.pdf
!provenance/nickel-iron/nifecurves.pdf
!provenance/silicon/sicurves.pdf
!provenance/stainless/sscurves.pdf
# The register of source documents itself stays a local file: it records where
# the maintainer's own copies of the third-party scans and books are held,
# which is not for publication. The papers cite every source. It is ignored
# here, not merely untracked, so a re-vendored release cannot bring it back.
provenance/SOURCES.md
# Likewise local, for the same reason: these two notebooks keep saved output
# cells that show the maintainer's own folder paths.
provenance/magnets/alnico_scanned/LNG40.nb
provenance/magnets/alnico_scanned/ProcessScannedCurve.nb
# An internal working note that names the maintainer's folder layout.
docs/pyfemm-inprocess-compat.md
# Maintainer working notes and scratch, kept local: the figure-regeneration
# notes (they drive scripts outside the repository), two handoff/procedure
# notes, an unbuilt debug program and a leftover test file.
manual/dialogs.md
docs/bdwgc-handoff-plan.md
docs/macos-verification.md
solvers/common/find_close.cpp
testing/myTestProblem.tmp
# The maintainer's working table of which block integrals return real or
# complex values, by physics; kept and edited locally.
docs/mo_blockintegral_cases.xlsx
*.png
!gui/icons/*.png
# The manual's figures are sources, not build products: since the manual moved
# from dvips to pdflatex they are PNG rather than PostScript, and the build
# fails without them.
!manual/*.png
*.zip
*.docx

# LaTeX intermediate files
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.dvi

# Compiled manual output
manual/manual.ps
manual/Release/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# Editor/OS artifacts
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code local config
.claude/

# Written into the source zip by packaging/buildsource.bat (a build from the
# zip has no .git to ask); never part of the repository itself.
/BUILD_NUMBER
